3. **`void` returns on fallible operations.** `parse` "validates" but can't report a validation failure; `save`/`load` do disk I/O but can't report I/O errors. Callers have no way to know whether anything succeeded.

4. **Presentation format baked into the model.** `render` hardcodes markdown as a method of `Report`, coupling the data model to one output format.

5. **Won't compile as-is.** `std::string` and `std::ostream` are used with no `#include <string>` / `#include <ostream>` (and no header file exists for this class).

